<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Sept output seen up +3.8 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Sept output seen up +3.8 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank economists expect Dutch September manufacturing production data, due on Wednesday morning, to show a strong year-on-year rise.</p>
<p>Their forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date--Period-Indicator------------Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p>0830 20/11 Sept   Manufac. output m/m  +0.8 pct   -0.9/+3.4 +2.0</p>
<p>0830 20/11 Sept   Manufac. output y/y  +3.8 pct   +3.0/+6.7 +2.4</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
